course: dictionary
lesson: 6987
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and paper is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Wax crayons are wrapped in paper labels by machine» uses paper for the thin material that you write and draw on.
explain: Sometimes paper describes something else. In «a paper cone of fried crickets», paper tells you what the cone is made of, so it works like a describing word. Check by swapping in "made of paper": a cone made of paper still makes sense.
explain: At school, paper can mean a test or your written work. «Hand in your papers» means give in your work, not the newspaper. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in it.
fact: Paper is a thin material we write and draw on.
fact: Paper is made from wood pulp from trees, and it can be recycled.
fact: A paper can be a newspaper, a test, or a piece of school work.
fact: Papers can be documents, such as a passport.
fact: As a describing word, paper means made of paper, as in «a paper plane».
exercise: «At the end of a lesson, put books, pencils and papers back where they belong.» In this sentence, papers means | Food for goats | Trees growing in a forest | Wax for crayons | *Sheets of paper or written documents
exercise: «At a night market in Thailand a child buys a paper cone of fried crickets.» In this sentence, paper describes the cone. It means | A cone for ice cream | A cone that is loud | *A cone made of paper | A cone that is very old
exercise: Paper is made from which natural material? | *Wood pulp from trees | Metal | Sand | Stone
test: «Then the tactful Mole leaves a pencil and paper by him.» Here, paper means | A test | *The thin material you write and draw on | A newspaper | A paper plane
test: «The paper round in our street pays good money.» In a paper round, paper means | Crickets | Wax crayons | Trees | *Newspapers
exam: «Grandma keeps her important papers, like her passport, in a drawer.» What does papers mean here? | Tests from school | Thin sheets for drawing | *Documents, such as a passport | Paper bags for shopping
